    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d34">

                <pb facs="0144" n="112" xml:id="pg112"/>

                <head>34. National Security Action Memorandum No. 57<anchor n="0" xml:id="d34-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1961-06-28">June 28,
                    1961</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list type="to">
                    <head>TO</head>
                    <item>The Secretary of State</item>
                    <item>The Secretary of Defense</item>
                    <item>The Director, CIA</item>
                </list>
                <p>The President has approved the attached recommendation.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d34-f2"/></p>
                <p>The Special Group (5412 Committee) will perform the functions assigned in the
                    recommendation to the Strategic Resources Group.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d34-f3"
                    /></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">McGeorge Bundy</hi></signed><anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d34-f4"/></closer>


                <xi:include href="d34-a1.xml" xpointer="d34-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d34-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d34-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Kennedy Library, National Security Files, Meetings and Memoranda Series,
                    NSAM 57. Secret. A copy was sent to General Taylor.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d34-f2" n="1" xml:id="d34-f2-content">
                <p>The text printed below is identical to Recommendation No. 2 of the Taylor Report
                    (see <ref target="#d32-f3">footnote 2, Document 32)</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d34-f3" n="2" xml:id="d34-f3-content">
                <p>Recommendation No. 1 of the Taylor Report called for creation of a Strategic
                    Resources Group (SRG), with its own permanent staff, as a mechanism for
                    planning, development, and coordination of Cold War strategy and individual
                    operations. According to a memorandum for the record by Burke, a member of the
                    Cuban Study Group, of a meeting the President held with the Group on June 13,
                    the President “was quite taken with” the SRG proposal as outlined to him by
                    Taylor, while Burke warned the President of “great danger” because if the SRG
                    Chairman “became an assistant President, it would be very difficult to operate
                    with State and Defense.” He noted that the President listened to this, but he
                    concluded: “I think he discounted the difficulties a great deal.” (Naval
                    Historical Center, Area Files, Bumpy Road Materials)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d34-f4" n="3" xml:id="d34-f4-content">
                <p>Printed from a copy that bears this typed signature.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
